<article class="env-lemma" id="0AZX">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0AZX">Lemma <span data-tag="0AZX">43.15.3</span>.</a> Let $A$ be a Noetherian local ring. Let $I \subset A$ be an ideal of definition. Let $M$ be a finite $A$-module. Let $d \geq \dim (\text{Supp}(M))$. Then </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  e_ I(M, d) = \sum \text{length}_{A_\mathfrak p}(M_\mathfrak p) e_ I(A/\mathfrak p, d)  \]
</div>
  <p> where the sum is over primes $\mathfrak p \subset A$ with $\dim (A/\mathfrak p) = d$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Both the left and side and the right hand side are additive in short exact sequences of modules of dimension $\leq d$, see Lemma <a href="/tag/0AZW" data-tag="0AZW">43.15.2</a> and Algebra, Lemma <a href="/tag/00IV" data-tag="00IV">10.52.3</a>. Hence by Algebra, Lemma <a href="/tag/00L0" data-tag="00L0">10.62.1</a> it suffices to prove this when $M = A/\mathfrak q$ for some prime $\mathfrak q$ of $A$ with $\dim (A/\mathfrak q) \leq d$. This case is obvious. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>